        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/uxm266/{size}/1966_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-11-23T15:41:18.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"LCinn\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lcinn/48/2659_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> LCinn:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I have often wondered how a time-travelling ranger would end up being the nemesis of plaguerat (how come we've known about chrono ranger's name such a long time? Did they spoil it?). I love the answer, it's a really cool hero-villain relation, different from the usual.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>His name was mentioned in one of the Plague Rats quote, and his face appeared on same card.</p>\n<p>Also, he wants <strong>REVENGE!</strong> giant rats took his arm, and when he heard of a giant rat terrorizing the world? Well, he coulnd't give up the opportunity!</p>",
